{
  "pedal": "Boss RT-2 Rotary Ensemble (mono in: INPUT A; stereo out: OUTPUT A and B), second session",
  "comment": "Rotor isolation (Balance 7:00 = the drum alone, 5:00 = the horn alone: measured -40 to -59 dB on the other rotor in the first session) with long white noise at Slow 9:00, per Mode; the mono output (OUTPUT B unplugged); the speed change between the extremes (stop and Fast 5:00, Rise/Fall FAST); then with the rotors stopped (Slow 7:00): the input clip in 0.5 dB steps, the output at Level 5:00, and per Drive position and Mode bursts (441 Hz, as in the first session) and noise at eight levels, plus a soft-loud-soft jump at Drive 9:00 (the soft notes' 2nd harmonic). Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise. Knob 1: Level (inner), Drive/Balance (outer; the Drive Knob toggle on top picks which stored value the ring sets; both act all the time). Knob 2: Fast (inner), Slow (outer). Toggles on top: Mode, Rise/Fall, Drive Knob. LED green = rotors slow, red = fast; change it by holding the RT-2's own pedal. Takes ordered for the fewest knob turns.",
